        "format": "guide",
        "title": "Lease-worker incident guide",
        "markdown": "# Lease-worker incident guide\n\n## What expiry means\n\nA lease expires after thirty seconds. Lease expiry does not prove that the former worker stopped.\n\n## Safe retry\n\nA fencing token lets storage reject writes from workers holding an older token. A retry acquires a new token before it writes. The retry must not assume that the former worker has stopped. Lease expiry alone never proves that the former worker stopped.\n\n## Trace rejection\n\nOperations should log the token on each write attempt so a stale rejection can be traced.\n",
